{title: When the Roll Is Called Up Yonder}
{artist: James M. Black}
{genre: Gospel}
{flow: Closing}
{style: Traditional}
{key: C}
{key_original: Ab}
{tempo: 100}
{time: 4/4}
{score: when-the-roll-is-called-up-yonder.abc}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
When the [C]trumpet of the Lord shall sound, and [F]time shall be no [C]more
And the [C]morning breaks, e[F]ternal, bright and [G7]fair
When the [C]saved of earth shall gather over [F]on the other [C]shore
And the [C]roll is called up [G7]yonder, I'll be [C]there
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
When the [C]roll is called up yonder, when the roll is called up yonder
When the [F]roll is called up [C]yonder, when the roll is called up yonder
When the [C]roll is called up [G7]yonder, I'll be [C]there
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
On that [C]bright and cloudless morning when the [F]dead in Christ shall [C]rise
And the [C]glory of His re[F]surrection [G7]share
When His [C]chosen ones shall gather to their [F]home beyond the [C]skies
And the [C]roll is called up [G7]yonder, I'll be [C]there
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Let us [C]labor for the Master from the [F]dawn till setting [C]sun
Let us [C]talk of all His [F]wondrous love and [G7]care
Then when [C]all of life is over, and our [F]work on earth is [C]done
And the [C]roll is called up [G7]yonder, I'll be [C]there
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
